2026-09-27T09:10:30.4704530Z Update Note
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4713300Z ===========
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4713770Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4714191Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4714351Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4714704Z ================
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4714948Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4715235Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4715886Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4716271Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4716472Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4716951Z ====================================
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4717269Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4717502Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4718557Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4719151Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4720233Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4721096Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4721263Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4721939Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4722788Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4723248Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4723639Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4724021Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4724100Z Packages
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4724282Z ========
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4724387Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4725659Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4726969Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4791507Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4792385Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4793742Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4794931Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4795825Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4796517Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4797160Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4797338Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4797760Z ==========================
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4798005Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4800157Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4802212Z 
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4803356Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4804897Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T09:10:30.4805259Z 
